===Etymology 1===
Shortened from {{m|en|woken}} or {{m|en|woken up}}, or derived from dialectal use of {{m|en||woke|pos=past participle of ''wake''}}. The sense of being aware of social injustice dates to at least the 1930s. The derogatory use has been most commonly used as of the 2020s.

